# Response headers for the static assets, applied by Cloudflare Workers.
# This is the Cloudflare equivalent of what server/static.ts does for the
# Fastify server, and it is load-bearing, not hygiene.
#
# The stage runs in <iframe sandbox="allow-scripts">, which gives it an opaque
# origin, and module scripts are always fetched in CORS mode. Without
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin the iframe cannot load its own bundle and the
# stage silently stays blank — no error a kid or we would ever see.
#
# frame-ancestors stops another site from framing runtime.html to run code at
# this origin. runtime-host/main.ts also refuses to run unless its own origin
# is opaque, but that is a client-side check; this one is the server's.
/runtime.html
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'

/assets/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
